% ============================================================================
% plant-life-cycle — each stage of a flowering plant's early life cycle as
% a NUMBER (1-3), the position in the ordered sequence
% (adj-facts-stdlib, BIOLOGY).
% ============================================================================
% A sibling library to the already-shipped `monarch-life-cycle.adj` and
% `frog-life-cycle.adj` — the SAME plain numbered life-cycle-stage recall
% shape, applied to a DIFFERENT organism. A flowering plant begins life as
% a seed, then germinates, then emerges above the soil as a seedling.
% Recall is a binding query:
%
%     ? plant_life_stage(germination, $N)   % 2
%
% A native `table` (ADJ-TABLES RS-5): each `row` lowers to a ground relation
% `plant_life_stage(stage, order)` carrying the source citation, so the
% lookup above is the ordinary SLD binding query — the engine returns the
% position WITH its source, on the CPU, with zero model calls, and abstains
% on a word that is not one of the three stages the source names. The query
% also runs BACKWARD — bind a number and recall the stage:
%
%     ? plant_life_stage($S, 1)   % seed
%
% The three stages IN ORDER, as a little truth table:
%
%     stage         order   quote (verbatim)
%     -----------   -----   --------------------------------------------------------------
%     seed          1       "They begin their lives as seeds."
%     germination   2       "When a seed begins to grow, this is called germination."
%     seedling      3       "When the first sign of life appears above the soil, this is
%                             called a sprout or seedling."
%
% Provenance: quoted verbatim from Ducksters' "Flowering Plants" (Biology
% for Kids) article's "Life-cycle of a Flowering Plant" section, which
% describes the stages in this order. WebFetch-verified before writing.
% `trust consensus` — this is the FIRST citation from Ducksters in this
% stdlib: a reputable, long-running kids-science-education site, the same
% tier this stdlib already reserves for other non-.gov kids-education
% sources (National Geographic Kids, Grammarly), not a primary .gov
% source. The source's own narrative goes on to describe a "mature plant"
% stage and "flowering," but this table deliberately does NOT extend past
% the first three stages, keeping this slice the same size as every
% sibling life-cycle library. A word that is NOT one of these three
% stages — `flowering`, a real later stage the source does describe, but
% not one this table's three rows number — is deliberately NOT a row, so
% a recall ABSTAINS on it rather than inventing a position. (See
% ../README.md; feedback_nothing_human_authored,
% feedback_adj_only_shipped_artifacts.)
% ============================================================================

table plant_life_stage {
    columns stage, order

    row (seed, 1)
    row (germination, 2)
    row (seedling, 3)

    source "They begin their lives as seeds."
    locator "https://www.ducksters.com/science/biology/flowering_plants.php"
    trust consensus
}
